Clock problem.
The first watch is 2 minutes fast per hour compared to standard time, and the second watch is 6 minutes fast per hour; thus, the second watch is $6-2=4$ minutes faster per hour than the first watch;
Every $60 \div 4=15$ hours, the minute hands of the first and second watches point in the same direction;
