meta.gold_solution:
**Analysis:**  
1 year = 12 months, to convert 2 years into months, multiply 12 by 2;  
1 day = 24 hours, to convert 48 hours into days, divide 48 by 24;  
1 week = 7 days, to convert 6 weeks into days, multiply 7 by 6;  
March, May, July, and August are months with 31 days, April and June are months with 30 days, then add up the days accordingly;  
In a leap year, February has 29 days, while in a common year, February has 28 days;  
There are 12 months in a year, among them January, March, May, July, August, October, and December have 31 days, April, June, September, and November have 30 days, February is a special month with 28 days in a common year and 29 days in a leap year.

- 2 years = $ \boxed{24}$ months;
- 48 hours = $ \boxed{2}$ days;
- 6 weeks = $ \boxed{42}$ days;
- From March to August totals $ \boxed{184}$ days;
- In a leap year, February has $ \boxed{29}$ days, while in a common year, February has $ \boxed{28}$ days;
- In a year, there are $ \boxed{7}$ months with 31 days, and $ \boxed{4}$ months with 30 days.

